Link the natives against Arch's system libopus and libpcre2.

audiopus_sys: Arch ships no libopus.a, so switch the crate to its `dynamic`
feature and hand its build script LIBOPUS_LIB_DIR=/usr. find_installed_opus()
then short-circuits build_opus(), so the vendored Opus tree is never
cmake-built; upstream's own OPUS_NO_PKG=1 keeps pkg-config out of the loop.
The remaining cmake/msvc env keys stay in place, inert.

pcre2-sys: only offers pkg-config discovery, so flip upstream's
PCRE2_SYS_STATIC from 1 to 0 (0 is an explicit "not static", not merely unset)
and let it probe libpcre2-8 from /usr.

Hunks are deliberately zero-context: MODULE.bazel's comments and neighbouring
env keys churn on nearly every upstream release, while each anchor line below
is unique in its file. patch locates a hunk by its replaced line alone, so
unrelated edits around them cannot break this patch.

--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -244 +244 @@
-audiopus_sys = { version = "0.2.2", features = ["static"] }
+audiopus_sys = { version = "0.2.2", features = ["dynamic"] }
--- a/MODULE.bazel
+++ b/MODULE.bazel
@@ -163 +163,3 @@
-        "CMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM": "3.5",
+        "CMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM": "3.5",
+        # Link Arch's shared /usr/lib/libopus.so instead of vendored Opus.
+        "LIBOPUS_LIB_DIR": "/usr",
@@ -192 +192 @@
-    build_script_env = {"PCRE2_SYS_STATIC": "1"},
+    build_script_env = {"PCRE2_SYS_STATIC": "0"},
